---
description: Feature tests make one HTTP request — seed state, do not chain requests
alwaysApply: true
---

# One HTTP request per test

A test method hits the app **once**. Setup is factories, `RateLimiter::hit`, `actingAs`, `config()`, not a previous `$this->get` / `post` / `call`.

Two requests hide which call failed, couple tests to leftover state, and are slower. Duplicate/idempotent/throttle cases seed the precondition, then one request.

```php
// BAD — first POST is setup
$this->postCapture($token, $body, $headers)->assertAccepted();
$this->postCapture($token, $body, $headers)->assertOk();

// GOOD — seed, then one POST
EndpointEvent::factory()->create([
    'endpoint_id' => $endpoint->id,
    'deduplication_key' => 'evt_dup',
    'payload' => $body,
]);
$this->postCapture($token, $body, $headers)->assertOk();
```

```php
// BAD — first POST fills the limiter
$this->postCapture($token, $body, $headers)->assertNotFound();
$this->postCapture($token, $body, $headers)->assertTooManyRequests();

// GOOD — seed the bucket Laravel will check (named limiter `capture` hashes `md5($name.$by)`)
config(['hookline.capture.rate_limit_per_minute' => 1]);
RateLimiter::hit(md5('capture'.$token));
$this->postCapture($token, $body, $headers)->assertTooManyRequests();
```

Livewire: one `Livewire::test()` **or** one HTTP call, not both as setup. `->call()` / `->set()` on that testable is fine — that is the component under test, not a second request used to seed state.

```php
// BAD — HTTP to create the row, then Livewire
$this->actingAs($user);
$this->post('/endpoints', ['name' => 'Stripe']);
Livewire::test(Index::class)->assertSee('Stripe');

// GOOD — factory, then one Livewire::test()
Endpoint::factory()->for($user)->create(['name' => 'Stripe']);
Livewire::test(Index::class)->assertSee('Stripe');
```
